---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The Goat's First Year — Daf Yomi Game: Bekhorot 20"
  description="Bekhorot 20: find the hidden hinge behind five readings of Rabbi Yishmael and Rabbi Yehoshua, watch a goat's year turn on a ring calendar around Ze'eiri's thirty days, swap the nameplates on the milk dispute, and breed ten kids into the tithe pen within a year."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@400;500;700;900&display=swap"
  />

  <main class="frank min-h-screen bg-[#15130e] !text-[#ece5d6]">
    <!-- ============ Hero ============ -->
    <header class="px-4 pt-12 pb-8">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-sm !text-[#a39a86]">
          <a href="/daf" class="underline decoration-[#4a4232] hover:!text-[#d9b26a]">Daf Yomi Arcade</a>, Bekhorot 20, 8 October 2026
        </p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 text-5xl font-black leading-[1.05] sm:text-6xl">The Goat's First Year</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-2xl !text-[#d9b26a]" dir="rtl" lang="he">אֵין טִינּוּף פָּחוֹת מִשְּׁלֹשִׁים יוֹם</p>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed !text-[#d6cdb9]">
          A Jew buys a young goat from a gentile, and nobody knows whether she has ever given birth. Did a
          <em>tinuf</em>, a murky discharge that counts as a birth, already "open her womb"? Today's daf finds the hidden
          hinge under one dispute five different ways, counts a goat's year down to the last day, swaps two sages'
          names, and fills a tithe pen from a single kid.
        </p>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 600 90" class="mt-6 w-full" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M10 78 H590" stroke="#4a4232" stroke-width="2" />
          <g stroke="#6b5f45" stroke-width="3">
            <path d="M40 78 V40 M90 78 V40 M140 78 V40 M190 78 V40 M240 78 V40" />
            <path d="M36 50 H244 M36 66 H244" />
          </g>
          <g fill="#d9b26a">
            <ellipse cx="380" cy="52" rx="34" ry="16" />
            <rect x="356" y="62" width="5" height="16" /><rect x="368" y="62" width="5" height="16" />
            <rect x="390" y="62" width="5" height="16" /><rect x="402" y="62" width="5" height="16" />
            <circle cx="420" cy="38" r="11" />
            <path d="M416 28 l-6 -12 M424 28 l4 -12" stroke="#d9b26a" stroke-width="3" />
            <path d="M424 48 l2 9" stroke="#d9b26a" stroke-width="3" />
          </g>
          <g fill="#9cc39a">
            <ellipse cx="480" cy="64" rx="15" ry="8" /><circle cx="496" cy="56" r="6" />
            <rect x="470" y="68" width="3" height="10" /><rect x="486" y="68" width="3" height="10" />
          </g>
          <text x="140" y="32" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#a39a86">the tithe pen</text>
          <text x="530" y="40" text-anchor="middle" font-size="22" fill="#ece5d6">?</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-20">
      <!-- ============ Part I: hinges ============ -->
      <section class="border-t border-[#3a3426] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p1">
        <h2 id="p1" class="text-3xl font-bold">I. Find the hinge</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#d6cdb9]">
          A baraita (20a:3–5) sets out three positions on the goat bought from a gentile. Rabbi Yishmael: if she gives birth
          within her first year, that kid certainly goes to the kohen. Rabbi Yehoshua: "You erred." A <em>tinuf</em> also
          exempts. And he adds his own view on top of the one he heard from the Rabbis. The Gemara keeps asking what the two sides
          <em>really</em> disagree about, and it finds a different hidden hinge each time. In every round, pick the hinge.
          Hinges that both sides already agree on are locked.
        </p>
        <div id="hinges" class="mt-5 space-y-5"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Part II: milk ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#3a3426] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p2">
        <h2 id="p2" class="text-3xl font-bold">II. Whose name goes on the milk?</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#d6cdb9]">
          Rabbi Akiva has his own rule: known to have given birth, the kohen gets nothing; known not to, the kid goes to the kohen; in doubt,
          the owner eats it once it is blemished (20b:3). So how is he different from Rabbi Yehoshua?
        </p>
        <div id="milk" class="mt-5 space-y-5"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Part III: pen ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#3a3426] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p3">
        <h2 id="p3" class="text-3xl font-bold">III. Ten in the pen</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#d6cdb9]">
          The animal tithe needs ten animals born in the same year. A baraita (20b:8): a young kid bore three daughters,
          and each daughter bore three, so all of them go into the pen to be tithed. Rabbi Shimon says, "I saw one that was tithed
          within her own year." Set the litters (up to triplets, as in the baraita) and get ten newborns into the pen.
        </p>
        <div id="pen" class="mt-5"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Score + learn ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#3a3426] pt-8" aria-labelledby="sc">
        <h2 id="sc" class="text-3xl font-bold">Your tally</h2>
        <p id="tally" class="mt-2 text-lg !text-[#d6cdb9]" aria-live="polite">Play the three parts above.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#3a3426] pt-8" aria-labelledby="learn">
        <h2 id="learn" class="text-3xl font-bold">Learn the real daf</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#d6cdb9]">
          Bekhorot 20 opens by finishing yesterday's cliffhanger. Rava says Rabbi Yishmael follows Rabbi Meir and worries about the minority.
          Ravina says the Rabbis don't follow a majority when it depends on an act, like whether a young goat has mated (20a:1–2).
          Then comes the baraita of Rabbi Yishmael, Rabbi Yehoshua and Rabbi Akiva, played above. Rashi and Rabbeinu Gershom
          work through the calendar arithmetic of 20a:11–20b:2 day by day.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-sm">
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.20a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#d9b26a]/50 px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#d9b26a] hover:border-[#d9b26a]">Bekhorot 20 on Sefaria ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rabbeinu_Gershom_on_Bekhorot.20a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a3426] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a39a86] hover:border-[#d9b26a]">Rabbeinu Gershom ×36 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Bekhorot.20a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a3426] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a39a86] hover:border-[#d9b26a]">Rashi ×31 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Steinsaltz_on_Bekhorot.20a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a3426] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a39a86] hover:border-[#d9b26a]">Steinsaltz ×22 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chidushei_Halachot_on_Bekhorot.20a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a3426] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a39a86] hover:border-[#d9b26a]">Maharsha, Chidushei Halachot ×9 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Bekhorot.20a.1.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a3426] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a39a86] hover:border-[#d9b26a]">Tosafot ×6 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Tosefta_Bekhorot.2.6" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a3426] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a39a86] hover:border-[#d9b26a]">Tosefta Bekhorot 2 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot.119a.2" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a3426] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a39a86] hover:border-[#d9b26a]">Yevamot 119a ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Mishneh_Torah,_Firstlings.4.10" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a3426] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a39a86] hover:border-[#d9b26a]">Rambam, Firstlings 4:10 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Shulchan_Arukh,_Yoreh_De'ah.315.7" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a3426] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a39a86] hover:border-[#d9b26a]">Shulchan Arukh YD 315:7 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.21a.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a3426] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a39a86] hover:border-[#d9b26a]">Continue: Bekhorot 21a ↗</a>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm !text-[#7d745f]">
          Part of the <a href="/daf" class="underline decoration-[#4a4232] hover:!text-[#a39a86]">Daf Yomi Arcade</a>,
          a new game from every daf. Texts and links via the Sefaria API.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <style is:global>
    .frank { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; }
    .act, .opt, .hg, .lit {
      border-radius: 0.4rem;
      border: 1px solid #5a5040;
      background: #15130e;
      color: #ece5d6;
      padding: 0.5rem 0.9rem;
      font-size: 1rem;
      transition: border-color 0.15s, background-color 0.15s, transform 0.15s;
    }
    .opt, .hg { text-align: left; }
    .act:hover:not(:disabled), .opt:hover:not(:disabled), .hg:hover:not(:disabled), .lit:hover:not(:disabled) { border-color: #d9b26a; }
    .act:focus-visible, .opt:focus-visible, .hg:focus-visible, .lit:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #d9b26a; outline-offset: 2px; }
    .act:disabled, .opt:disabled, .hg:disabled, .lit:disabled { opacity: 0.55; cursor: default; }
    .hg.locked { opacity: 0.45; border-style: dashed; }
    .ok { border-color: #9cc39a !important; background: #1b2a1c !important; opacity: 1 !important; }
    .bad { border-color: #c46a5a !important; background: #2e1a17 !important; opacity: 1 !important; }
    .card { border-radius: 0.5rem; border: 1px solid #3a3426; background: #1c1912; padding: 1rem; }
    .side { border-radius: 0.4rem; border: 1px solid #3a3426; padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; }
    .lit { padding: 0.3rem 0; min-width: 2.4rem; text-align: center; }
    .lit[aria-pressed='true'] { border-color: #d9b26a; background: #33291a; }
    .tab { border-bottom: 2px solid transparent; padding: 0.3rem 0.5rem; }
    .tab[aria-selected='true'] { border-color: #d9b26a; }
    .plate { display: inline-block; border-radius: 0.3rem; padding: 0.25rem 0.7rem; background: #33291a; border: 1px solid #d9b26a; font-weight: 700; transition: transform 0.6s; }
    .drop { animation: drop 0.5s ease-out; }
    @keyframes drop { from { transform: translateY(-14px); opacity: 0; } to { transform: none; opacity: 1; } }
    .crack { animation: crack 0.4s; }
    @keyframes crack { 25% { transform: translateX(-5px) rotate(-1deg); } 75% { transform: translateX(5px) rotate(1deg); } }
    .grow { transition: stroke-dashoffset 1.1s ease-out; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .act, .opt, .hg, .lit, .plate { transition: none !important; }
      .drop, .crack { animation: none !important; }
      .grow { transition: none !important; }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id)!;
    const sef = (ref: string) => `https://www.sefaria.org/${ref.replace(/ (\d+[ab]?):/, '.$1.').replace(/ /g, '_')}`;
    const link = (ref: string) =>
      `<a href="${sef(ref)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="!text-[#d9b26a] underline decoration-[#4a4232] hover:!text-[#f0d49a]">${ref} ↗</a>`;
    const good = (s: string) => `<p class="!text-[#bfe0bd]">✓ ${s}</p>`;
    const miss = (s: string) => `<p class="!text-[#f0c0b4]">✗ ${s}</p>`;
    const note = (s: string) => `<p class="!text-[#d6cdb9]">${s}</p>`;
    const score: Record<string, [number, number]> = { hinge: [0, 6], milk: [0, 4], pen: [0, 2] };
    const tally = () => {
      const got = Object.values(score).reduce((a, [g]) => a + g, 0);
      const max = Object.values(score).reduce((a, [, m]) => a + m, 0);
      const rank = got >= max - 2 ? 'Rabbi Shimon, who saw it with his own eyes' : got >= max / 2 ? 'a shepherd who counts to thirty' : 'still waiting on the murk';
      $('tally').innerHTML = `<span class="!text-[#d9b26a] font-bold">${got} / ${max}</span>. Ranked: ${rank}.`;
    };

    type Q = { q: string; opts: string[]; ans: number; why: string; ref: string };
    const ask = (host: HTMLElement, item: Q, bucket: string, after?: () => void) => {
      const div = document.createElement('div');
      div.className = 'card drop';
      div.innerHTML = `<p class="!text-[#ece5d6]">${item.q}</p><div class="mt-2 flex flex-col gap-1.5">${item.opts
        .map((o, j) => `<button class="opt text-sm" data-j="${j}">${o}</button>`)
        .join('')}</div><div class="out mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div>`;
      host.appendChild(div);
      div.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button.opt').forEach((b) =>
        b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const j = +b.dataset.j!;
          const right = j === item.ans;
          div.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button.opt').forEach((x) => {
            x.disabled = true;
            if (+x.dataset.j! === item.ans) x.classList.add('ok');
          });
          if (!right) { b.classList.add('bad'); div.classList.add('crack'); }
          else score[bucket][0]++;
          div.querySelector('.out')!.innerHTML = (right ? good(item.why) : miss(item.why)) + note(link(item.ref));
          tally();
          after?.();
        }),
      );
      return div;
    };

    // ================= Part I: hinges + ring calendar =================
    const HINGES = [
      'Does a tinuf that was actually seen exempt her?',
      'Do we worry about a tinuf that nobody saw?',
      'Can a goat that had a tinuf recover and still give birth in her first year?',
      'Ze\'eiri: after a tinuf, no pregnancy for thirty days',
      'Can an animal give birth after incomplete months?',
      'Is part of a day like a whole day?',
    ];
    type Path = { window: boolean; conceive: number; gest: number; birth: number; verdict: string; kohen: boolean };
    type Round = {
      title: string; ref: string; a: [string, string]; b: [string, string]; locked: number[]; ans: number;
      trap?: [number, string]; why: string; ring?: { A: Path; B: Path }; follow?: Q;
    };
    const B_CASE = 'The case: a goat has a tinuf at the end of her sixth month, then gives birth before her first year is out. A goat carries for five months.';
    const ROUNDS: Round[] = [
      {
        title: 'Round 1 · Rabbi Yishmael vs. Rabbi Yehoshua',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 20a:6-7',
        a: ['Rabbi Yishmael', 'She gave birth in her first year after we bought her, so that kid is certainly the kohen\'s.'],
        b: ['Rabbi Yehoshua', 'You erred. A tinuf also exempts, so the next kid stays with the owner as a doubt.'],
        locked: [], ans: 1,
        trap: [0, 'That is the Gemara\'s first guess ("shall we say…"), and it rejects it: if we actually see a tinuf, everyone agrees it exempts.'],
        why: 'Everyone agrees a tinuf they saw exempts her. The dispute is about worrying over one nobody saw. Rabbi Yishmael doesn\'t worry, so her first kid is a firstborn. Rabbi Yehoshua does worry, so it stays with the owner.',
        follow: {
          q: 'Rava objects: earlier he said Rabbi Yishmael follows Rabbi Meir and <em>does</em> worry about the minority. How does the Gemara answer?',
          opts: [
            'Rabbi Yishmael worries about a minority only when that leads to a stringency, and here it would lead to a leniency',
            'Rava withdrew his statement after hearing this baraita',
            'Rabbi Meir worries about the minority only for people, not animals',
          ],
          ans: 0,
          why: 'He worries only when the worry makes things stricter. Here, worrying about a tinuf would make the kid only a doubtful firstborn, which is a leniency.',
          ref: 'Bekhorot 20a:8',
        },
      },
      {
        title: 'Round 2 · Rabbi Yishmael vs. Rabbi Yehoshua, again',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 20a:9',
        a: ['Rabbi Yishmael', 'He does worry about a tinuf, whether that is lenient or strict. And still: certainly the kohen\'s.'],
        b: ['Rabbi Yehoshua', 'The next kid stays with the owner as a doubt.'],
        locked: [0, 1], ans: 2,
        why: 'Rabbi Yishmael holds that a goat that had a tinuf does not recover and give birth within her first year. So if she gave birth, she never had one. Rabbi Yehoshua holds that she can recover and give birth within the year.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Round 3 · Rabbi Yehoshua\'s report of the Rabbis vs. his own view',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 20a:10-12',
        a: ['The Rabbis (as he heard it)', 'The next male is not exempt. It is a firstborn.'],
        b: ['Rabbi Yehoshua himself', 'A goat that had a tinuf at six months can give birth within her first year, and the tinuf exempts.'],
        locked: [0, 1, 2], ans: 3,
        why: 'Ze\'eiri says a tinuf that exempts blocks pregnancy for at least thirty days (אֵין טִינּוּף פָּחוֹת מִשְּׁלֹשִׁים יוֹם). To give birth by the end of the year, this goat must have conceived within that month. The Rabbis accept Ze\'eiri, so that "tinuf" was never a fetus and the kid is a firstborn. Rabbi Yehoshua does not accept Ze\'eiri, so the tinuf counts.',
        ring: {
          A: { window: true, conceive: 196, gest: 150, birth: 346, kohen: true, verdict: 'Conceived inside Ze\'eiri\'s thirty days, so the tinuf was never a fetus. The next male is a <b>firstborn</b>.' },
          B: { window: false, conceive: 196, gest: 150, birth: 346, kohen: false, verdict: 'No thirty-day rule, so a pregnancy right after the tinuf is fine. The tinuf counts and she is <b>exempt</b>.' },
        },
      },
      {
        title: 'Round 4 · Same two, with Ze\'eiri agreed',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 20a:13-20b:1',
        a: ['The Rabbis (as he heard it)', 'Firstborn.'],
        b: ['Rabbi Yehoshua himself', 'Exempt.'],
        locked: [0, 1, 2, 3], ans: 4,
        why: 'Both accept Ze\'eiri. The Rabbis hold there are no early births, so a birth inside year one means she conceived inside the thirty days, and the next male is a firstborn. Rabbi Yehoshua holds an animal can give birth after incomplete months. She may have conceived after the thirty days and carried short, so the tinuf is real and she is exempt.',
        ring: {
          A: { window: true, conceive: 196, gest: 150, birth: 346, kohen: true, verdict: 'A full five months and still inside the year, so she conceived inside the thirty days. <b>Firstborn</b>.' },
          B: { window: true, conceive: 216, gest: 132, birth: 348, kohen: false, verdict: 'Conceived after the thirty days, then a short pregnancy. The tinuf is real and she is <b>exempt</b>.' },
        },
      },
      {
        title: 'Round 5 · Ze\'eiri agreed, no early births',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 20b:2',
        a: ['The Rabbis (as he heard it)', 'Firstborn.'],
        b: ['Rabbi Yehoshua himself', 'Exempt.'],
        locked: [0, 1, 2, 3, 4], ans: 5,
        why: 'It comes down to the last day. For Rabbi Yehoshua, part of a day counts as a whole day. She can conceive on the thirtieth day and give birth exactly five months later, just before the year ends, so she is exempt. The Rabbis do not count part of a day. The earliest such birth falls on the first day of year two, so a birth inside year one means she conceived inside the window, and the kid is a firstborn.',
        ring: {
          A: { window: true, conceive: 211, gest: 150, birth: 361, kohen: true, verdict: 'Day 30 doesn\'t count until it is over. Conceive on day 31 and five months lands on <b>year two</b>, so any birth inside year one was conceived in the window. <b>Firstborn</b>.' },
          B: { window: true, conceive: 210, gest: 150, birth: 360, kohen: false, verdict: 'Part of day 30 counts as all of it. Conceive then and give birth on the <b>last day of year one</b>. <b>Exempt</b>.' },
        },
      },
    ];

    // Ring geometry: 12 months of 30 days drawn as a dial, day 0 at the top.
    const CX = 150, CY = 150;
    const pt = (d: number, r: number) => {
      const t = (d / 360) * 2 * Math.PI - Math.PI / 2;
      return [CX + r * Math.cos(t), CY + r * Math.sin(t)];
    };
    const arc = (d0: number, d1: number, r: number) => {
      const [x0, y0] = pt(d0, r), [x1, y1] = pt(d1, r);
      return `M${x0.toFixed(1)} ${y0.toFixed(1)} A${r} ${r} 0 ${d1 - d0 > 180 ? 1 : 0} 1 ${x1.toFixed(1)} ${y1.toFixed(1)}`;
    };
    const ringSvg = (p: Path) => {
      const ticks = Array.from({ length: 12 }, (_, m) => {
        const [x0, y0] = pt(m * 30, 112), [x1, y1] = pt(m * 30, 124), [tx, ty] = pt(m * 30 + 15, 136);
        return `<line x1="${x0}" y1="${y0}" x2="${x1}" y2="${y1}" stroke="#5a5040"/><text x="${tx}" y="${ty + 4}" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#7d745f">${m + 1}</text>`;
      }).join('');
      const len = (2 * Math.PI * 88 * p.gest) / 360;
      const [bx, by] = pt(p.birth, 88), [cx, cy] = pt(p.conceive, 88), [tx, ty] = pt(180, 100);
      const late = p.birth > 360;
      return `<svg viewBox="0 0 300 300" class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[300px]" role="img" aria-label="Ring calendar of the goat's first year: tinuf at day 180, conception at day ${p.conceive}, birth at day ${p.birth}${late ? ', in year two' : ''}">
        <circle cx="${CX}" cy="${CY}" r="118" fill="none" stroke="#3a3426" stroke-width="2"/>
        ${ticks}
        <path d="${arc(0, 180, 104)}" stroke="#4a4232" stroke-width="6" fill="none"/>
        ${p.window ? `<path d="${arc(180, 210, 104)}" stroke="#c46a5a" stroke-width="10" fill="none" opacity="0.8"/>` : ''}
        <path class="grow" d="${arc(p.conceive, p.birth, 88)}" stroke="${p.kohen ? '#d9b26a' : '#9cc39a'}" stroke-width="7" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" ${p.gest < 150 ? 'stroke-dasharray="6 5"' : `stroke-dasharray="${len}" stroke-dashoffset="${len}"`}/>
        <circle cx="${tx}" cy="${ty}" r="5" fill="#a39a86"/>
        <circle cx="${cx}" cy="${cy}" r="5" fill="#ece5d6"/>
        <circle cx="${bx}" cy="${by}" r="8" fill="${late ? '#c46a5a' : p.kohen ? '#d9b26a' : '#9cc39a'}"/>
        <line x1="150" y1="20" x2="150" y2="44" stroke="#ece5d6" stroke-width="2"/>
        <text x="150" y="146" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#ece5d6">day ${p.birth > 360 ? '1 of year 2' : p.birth}</text>
        <text x="150" y="164" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#a39a86">tinuf day 180 · conceived ${p.conceive}</text>
        <text x="150" y="180" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#a39a86">${p.gest < 150 ? 'short pregnancy' : 'five full months'}</text>
      </svg>`;
    };

    const hingeHost = $('hinges');
    let roundIx = 0;
    const playRound = () => {
      const r = ROUNDS[roundIx];
      if (!r) {
        hingeHost.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend', `<div class="card drop">${note('Five readings, five hinges. The two sides never move: kohen versus owner. Only the reason underneath them changes.')}</div>`);
        startMilk();
        return;
      }
      const div = document.createElement('div');
      div.className = 'card drop';
      div.innerHTML = `<p class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide !text-[#d9b26a]">${r.title}</p>
        ${r.ring ? `<p class="mt-2 text-sm !text-[#d6cdb9]">${B_CASE}</p>` : ''}
        <div class="mt-3 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="side"><p class="font-bold !text-[#d9b26a]">${r.a[0]}</p><p class="text-sm !text-[#d6cdb9]">${r.a[1]}</p></div>
          <div class="side"><p class="font-bold !text-[#9cc39a]">${r.b[0]}</p><p class="text-sm !text-[#d6cdb9]">${r.b[1]}</p></div>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 !text-[#ece5d6]">What hinge do they really turn on?</p>
        <div class="mt-2 flex flex-col gap-1.5">${HINGES.map((h, j) => {
          const lk = r.locked.includes(j);
          return `<button class="hg text-sm ${lk ? 'locked' : ''}" data-j="${j}" ${lk ? 'disabled aria-label="' + h + ' (agreed by both)"' : ''}>${lk ? '🔒 ' : ''}${h}${lk ? ' <span class="!text-[#7d745f]">(agreed)</span>' : ''}</button>`;
        }).join('')}</div>
        <div class="out mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div>
        <div class="ring mt-3"></div>
        <div class="fol mt-3"></div>`;
      hingeHost.appendChild(div);
      const out = div.querySelector('.out')!;
      let firstTry = true;
      div.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button.hg:not(.locked)').forEach((b) =>
        b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const j = +b.dataset.j!;
          if (j !== r.ans) {
            firstTry = false;
            b.classList.add('bad');
            b.disabled = true;
            div.classList.remove('crack'); void div.offsetWidth; div.classList.add('crack');
            out.innerHTML = miss(r.trap && r.trap[0] === j ? r.trap[1] : 'Not that one. That hinge doesn\'t separate these two. Try again.');
            return;
          }
          div.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button.hg').forEach((x) => (x.disabled = true));
          b.classList.add('ok');
          if (firstTry) score.hinge[0]++;
          tally();
          out.innerHTML = (firstTry ? good(r.why) : note(r.why)) + note(link(r.ref));
          if (r.ring) drawRing(div.querySelector('.ring') as HTMLElement, r);
          const next = () => { roundIx++; playRound(); };
          if (r.follow) ask(div.querySelector('.fol') as HTMLElement, r.follow, 'hinge', next);
          else {
            const btn = document.createElement('button');
            btn.className = 'act mt-3 text-sm';
            btn.textContent = roundIx < ROUNDS.length - 1 ? 'Next reading →' : 'On to Rabbi Akiva →';
            btn.addEventListener('click', () => { btn.remove(); next(); });
            div.appendChild(btn);
          }
        }),
      );
    };
    const drawRing = (host: HTMLElement, r: Round) => {
      host.innerHTML = `<div role="tablist" class="flex justify-center gap-3 text-sm">
          <button role="tab" class="tab !text-[#d9b26a]" data-s="A" aria-selected="true">${r.a[0]}</button>
          <button role="tab" class="tab !text-[#9cc39a]" data-s="B" aria-selected="false">${r.b[0]}</button>
        </div><div class="dial mt-2"></div><p class="verdict mt-1 text-center text-sm !text-[#d6cdb9]" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-center text-xs !text-[#7d745f]">Twelve thirty-day months for the picture. The red band is Ze'eiri's thirty days after the tinuf.</p>`;
      const show = (s: 'A' | 'B') => {
        const p = r.ring![s];
        host.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[role=tab]').forEach((t) => t.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(t.dataset.s === s)));
        host.querySelector('.dial')!.innerHTML = ringSvg(p);
        host.querySelector('.verdict')!.innerHTML = p.verdict;
        const g = host.querySelector<SVGPathElement>('.grow');
        if (g && g.getAttribute('stroke-dashoffset')) requestAnimationFrame(() => requestAnimationFrame(() => g.setAttribute('stroke-dashoffset', '0')));
      };
      host.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[role=tab]').forEach((t) => t.addEventListener('click', () => show(t.dataset.s as 'A' | 'B')));
      show('A');
    };

    // ================= Part II: milk nameplates =================
    const milkHost = $('milk');
    let milkStarted = false;
    const startMilk = () => {
      if (milkStarted) return;
      milkStarted = true;
      ask(milkHost, {
        q: 'Rabbi Ḥanina of Sura: what practical case separates Rabbi Akiva from Rabbi Yehoshua?',
        opts: [
          'A goat seen having a tinuf at six months',
          'An animal that came into the Jew\'s hands already giving milk',
          'A donkey in her fourth year',
        ],
        ans: 1,
        why: '"Milk exempts" is between them (חָלָב פּוֹטֵר אִיכָּא בֵּינַיְיהוּ). Does an animal already in milk count as one that has given birth?',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 20b:4',
      }, 'milk', plates);
    };
    const plates = () => {
      const div = document.createElement('div');
      div.className = 'card drop';
      const SEATS = [
        { pos: 'Milk exempts. Follow the majority of animals, and most animals give no milk unless they have given birth.', who: 'Akiva' },
        { pos: 'There is a minority that gives milk without giving birth, so the next kid is a doubtful firstborn.', who: 'Yehoshua' },
      ];
      div.innerHTML = `<p class="!text-[#ece5d6]">As Rabbi Ḥanina first lays it out, whose nameplate goes on each position? Tap a position to set it.</p>
        <div class="mt-3 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2">${SEATS.map((s, i) => `<button class="opt seat text-sm" data-i="${i}"><span class="plate text-xs !text-[#d9b26a]" data-p="${i}">?</span><span class="mt-2 block !text-[#d6cdb9]">${s.pos}</span></button>`).join('')}</div>
        <button class="act lock mt-3 text-sm" disabled>Lock in</button>
        <div class="out mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div>`;
      milkHost.appendChild(div);
      const names = ['?', 'Rabbi Akiva', 'Rabbi Yehoshua'];
      const pick = [0, 0];
      const lock = div.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.lock')!;
      div.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.seat').forEach((b) =>
        b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const i = +b.dataset.i!;
          pick[i] = pick[i] === 1 ? 2 : 1;
          pick[1 - i] = pick[i] === 1 ? 2 : 1;
          div.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.plate').forEach((p) => (p.textContent = names[pick[+p.dataset.p!]]));
          lock.disabled = false;
        }),
      );
      lock.addEventListener('click', () => {
        lock.disabled = true;
        div.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.seat').forEach((x) => (x.disabled = true));
        const right = pick[0] === 1;
        if (right) score.milk[0]++;
        if (!right) { pick[0] = 1; pick[1] = 2; div.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.plate').forEach((p) => (p.textContent = names[pick[+p.dataset.p!]])); }
        tally();
        div.querySelector('.out')!.innerHTML =
          (right ? good('As first stated: Rabbi Akiva follows the majority, and milk exempts. Rabbi Yehoshua worries about the minority.') : miss('As first stated, Rabbi Akiva follows the majority (milk exempts) and Rabbi Yehoshua worries about the minority. Hold that thought.')) +
          note(link('Bekhorot 20b:4'));
        majority(div);
      });
    };
    const majority = (platesDiv: HTMLElement) => {
      const div = document.createElement('div');
      div.className = 'card drop';
      div.innerHTML = `<p class="!text-[#ece5d6]">But does Rabbi Yehoshua worry about a minority? Mishna Yevamot (119a): a childless widow's mother-in-law went overseas
        while pregnant. Must the widow worry that a brother-in-law was born, who would bind her to levirate marriage? Rabbi Yehoshua says she need not.
        Here is his arithmetic. Tap every slice that leaves her <b>free</b>, with no brother-in-law born.</p>
        <label class="mt-3 block text-sm !text-[#a39a86]">How many pregnancies miscarry (a minority, any size): <span class="mv !text-[#ece5d6]">10</span>%
          <input type="range" min="2" max="40" value="10" class="mr mt-1 w-full accent-[#d9b26a]" aria-label="Miscarriage share" /></label>
        <div class="bar mt-3 flex h-14 w-full overflow-hidden rounded-md border border-[#3a3426]"></div>
        <p class="sum mt-2 text-sm !text-[#d6cdb9]" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <button class="act chk mt-2 text-sm">Check</button>
        <div class="out mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div>`;
      milkHost.appendChild(div);
      const SL = [
        { k: 'mis', he: 'מַפִּילוֹת', en: 'miscarry', col: '#6b5f45' },
        { k: 'fem', he: 'נְקֵבוֹת', en: 'girls', col: '#7a6a8e' },
        { k: 'male', he: 'זְכָרִים', en: 'boys', col: '#4f6b4e' },
      ];
      const sel = new Set<string>();
      let m = 10, done = false;
      const render = () => {
        const w: Record<string, number> = { mis: m, fem: (100 - m) / 2, male: (100 - m) / 2 };
        div.querySelector('.bar')!.innerHTML = SL.map((s) => `<button class="slice flex flex-col items-center justify-center text-xs ${sel.has(s.k) ? 'ring-2 ring-inset ring-[#d9b26a]' : ''}" data-k="${s.k}" aria-pressed="${sel.has(s.k)}" style="width:${w[s.k]}%;background:${s.col}" ${done ? 'disabled' : ''}><span dir="rtl" lang="he" class="!text-[#ece5d6]">${s.he}</span><span class="!text-[#ece5d6]">${w[s.k].toFixed(0)}%</span></button>`).join('');
        const free = [...sel].reduce((a, k) => a + w[k], 0);
        div.querySelector('.sum')!.innerHTML = sel.size ? `Free: <b class="!text-[#d9b26a]">${free.toFixed(0)}%</b>. Bound to a levir: <b>${(100 - free).toFixed(0)}%</b>.` : 'Nothing selected yet.';
        div.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.slice').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => { const k = b.dataset.k!; sel.has(k) ? sel.delete(k) : sel.add(k); render(); }));
      };
      const range = div.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('.mr')!;
      range.addEventListener('input', () => { m = +range.value; div.querySelector('.mv')!.textContent = String(m); render(); });
      render();
      const chk = div.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.chk')!;
      chk.addEventListener('click', () => {
        done = true; chk.disabled = true;
        const right = sel.size === 2 && sel.has('mis') && sel.has('fem');
        if (right) score.milk[0]++;
        sel.clear(); sel.add('mis'); sel.add('fem'); render(); tally();
        div.querySelector('.out')!.innerHTML =
          (right ? good('Exactly.') : miss('The free slices are the miscarriages and the girls.')) +
          note('"Join the minority that miscarry to the half that are girls, and the boys are a minority. And we don\'t worry about a minority." Slide the miscarriage share anywhere: as long as it is more than zero, the boys stay under half.') +
          note(link('Bekhorot 20b:5-6'));
        swap(platesDiv);
      });
    };
    const swap = (platesDiv: HTMLElement) => {
      ask(milkHost, {
        q: 'So Rabbi Yehoshua doesn\'t worry about a minority, yet in Rabbi Ḥanina\'s version he worries that a milking animal might not have given birth. How does the Gemara fix it?',
        opts: [
          'Reverse them: Rabbi Yehoshua says milk exempts, and Rabbi Akiva says it does not',
          'Rabbi Yehoshua worries about a minority for animals but not for people',
          'Rabbi Ḥanina of Sura is rejected, and there is no difference between them',
        ],
        ans: 0,
        why: '"Rather, reverse it" (אֵיפוֹךְ), and a baraita teaches it that way: milk exempts, says Rabbi Yehoshua. Rabbi Akiva says milk does not exempt. Watch the nameplates trade places.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 20b:7',
      }, 'milk', () => {
        const ps = platesDiv.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.plate');
        const reduce = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
        ps.forEach((p, i) => { if (!reduce) p.style.transform = `translateY(-8px) rotate(${i ? 6 : -6}deg)`; });
        setTimeout(() => {
          ps.forEach((p) => { p.textContent = +p.dataset.p! === 0 ? 'Rabbi Yehoshua' : 'Rabbi Akiva'; p.style.transform = ''; p.style.background = '#1b2a1c'; p.style.borderColor = '#9cc39a'; });
        }, reduce ? 0 : 450);
        startPen();
      });
    };

    // ================= Part III: ten in the pen =================
    let penStarted = false;
    const startPen = () => {
      if (penStarted) return;
      penStarted = true;
      const host = $('pen');
      host.innerHTML = `<div class="card drop">
        <p class="!text-[#ece5d6]">Litter sizes. The mother kid's daughters are all female, and each can bear in turn.</p>
        <div class="mt-3"><p class="text-sm font-bold !text-[#d9b26a]">The mother kid</p><div class="ml flex gap-1.5" role="group" aria-label="Mother's litter"></div></div>
        <div class="dts mt-3 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-3"></div>
        <div class="kids mt-4 flex min-h-[2.5rem] flex-wrap gap-1 rounded-md border border-dashed border-[#5a5040] p-2" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <p class="cnt mt-2 !text-[#d6cdb9]" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <button class="act again mt-2 text-sm">Let the mother give birth again this year</button>
        <div class="out mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div>
        <div class="qs mt-3 space-y-4"></div>
      </div>`;
      let mom = 0, second = 0;
      const d = [0, 0, 0];
      let hitTen = false, triedAgain = false;
      const qs = host.querySelector('.qs') as HTMLElement;
      const out = host.querySelector('.out')!;
      const litBtns = (val: number, name: string) => [0, 1, 2, 3].map((n) => `<button class="lit" data-n="${n}" data-w="${name}" aria-pressed="${n === val}">${n}</button>`).join('');
      const render = () => {
        host.querySelector('.ml')!.innerHTML = litBtns(mom, 'm');
        host.querySelector('.dts')!.innerHTML = Array.from({ length: Math.min(mom, 3) }, (_, i) => `<div class="side"><p class="text-sm !text-[#9cc39a]">Daughter ${i + 1}</p><div class="mt-1 flex gap-1" role="group" aria-label="Daughter ${i + 1} litter">${litBtns(d[i], String(i))}</div></div>`).join('');
        const total = mom + second + d.slice(0, mom).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
        host.querySelector('.kids')!.innerHTML = Array.from({ length: total }, (_, i) => `<span class="drop text-xl" title="kid ${i + 1}">${i < mom + second ? '🐐' : '🐑'}</span>`).join('') || '<span class="text-sm !text-[#7d745f]">empty pen</span>';
        host.querySelector('.cnt')!.innerHTML = `Born this year: <b class="${total >= 10 ? '!text-[#9cc39a]' : '!text-[#d9b26a]'}">${total}</b> / 10${total >= 10 ? '. Into the pen to be tithed!' : ''}`;
        host.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.lit').forEach((b) =>
          b.addEventListener('click', () => {
            const n = +b.dataset.n!, w = b.dataset.w!;
            if (w === 'm') mom = n; else d[+w] = n;
            for (let i = mom; i < 3; i++) d[i] = 0;
            render();
          }),
        );
        if (total >= 10 && !second && !hitTen) { hitTen = true; reached(); }
      };
      const reached = () => {
        out.innerHTML = good('Ten in a single year, from a single kid. That is what Rabbi Shimon saw.') + note(link('Bekhorot 20b:8'));
        ask(qs, {
          q: 'Ten only needs 3 + 3 + 2 + 2: the mother bears three, one daughter three, the other two daughters twins. So why does the baraita have every daughter bear three?',
          opts: [
            'Because one of them has to bear three anyway, the baraita kept it uniform: three each',
            'Because the tithe actually needs twelve animals',
            'Because twins don\'t count for the tithe',
          ],
          ans: 0,
          why: 'One of the goats can\'t make it without triplets, so the baraita gave all three daughters triplets for consistency.',
          ref: 'Bekhorot 20b:8-9',
        }, 'pen');
      };
      const again = host.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.again')!;
      again.addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (triedAgain) return;
        triedAgain = true;
        again.disabled = true;
        mom = 3; d[0] = 2; d[1] = 2; d[2] = 2; second = 1;
        render();
        out.innerHTML = note('The Gemara tries exactly this: three daughters bear twins each, and the mother bears one more alongside them. 3 + 6 + 1 = 10, with no triplets in the second generation.');
        ask(qs, {
          q: 'The baraita didn\'t teach this easier case. What does its silence prove?',
          opts: [
            'A goat does not give birth twice within the same year',
            'A mother and her daughters can\'t be tithed together',
            'Kids born to the mother count for the previous year',
          ],
          ans: 0,
          why: 'Since the baraita didn\'t use the simpler route, a goat must not give birth again within the same year. The extra 🐐 goes back out of the pen.',
          ref: 'Bekhorot 20b:9',
        }, 'pen', () => { second = 0; d[0] = 3; d[1] = 3; d[2] = 3; render(); });
      });
      render();
    };

    playRound();
    tally();
  </script>
</Layout>
